## Delivered

T04 changes no product code. The diff is three new test files, two existing test
files, the test manifest, the three active guidance documents, and the evidence
record.

- `tests/Persistence.Tests/EndToEnd/ClientIntakeWorkflowPersistenceTests.cs`
  (new) — the real `AccountantIntakeWorkflow` and `ClientIntakeWorkflow` driving
  the real `SqlIntakeStore` and `SqlReviewRecordRepository`, through the approved
  `InternalsVisibleTo("Persistence.Tests")` seam, against a real relational
  database with the real `20260730000000_AddClientIntake` migration applied. Each
  store call gets its own context, mirroring the portal's scoped registration, so
  no EF identity map can answer a read the database never saw.
- `tests/TaxAI.Portal.Tests/EndToEnd/ClientIntakeAcceptanceTests.cs` (new) and
  `ClientIntakeSecurityAcceptanceTests.cs` (new) — the real portal composition
  over HTTP: routing, rate limiting, authentication, R-1 authorization,
  antiforgery, the cookie protector, the multipart transport, both real
  workflows, the real `CryptographicIntakeCredentialSource`, the real
  `DevelopmentEncryptedIntakeContentStore`, and every Razor component. Two firms
  run over one shared intake store, so a cross-firm read is a real cross-firm
  read rather than a lookup in an empty dictionary.
- Only two collaborators are substituted in the portal suite — the intake
  metadata store and the review-record repository — because the real ones are SQL
  Server. Those exact adapters are the ones exercised for real in the persistence
  suite, so no part of the shipped path is represented by a double in both.
- `tests/TaxAI.Portal.Tests/EndToEnd/SolutionAndRegressionTests.cs` gains the
  excluded-capability, retention, and single-content-store-implementation scans.
  `RepositoryVerificationTests.cs` gains the completed-guidance and
  per-criterion-evidence checks and pins the portal's exact five-reference set.
- `specs/014-client-intake-and-document-upload-flow/verification.md` (new)
  records AC-1 through AC-99 with named tests, the authoritative gate totals, the
  raw-byte exception stated plainly, and what remains gated.
- `README.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, and `NEXT.md` record spec 014 as complete without
  moving a gate.

## Proven

- the synthetic happy path to `Ready` and the exact review handoff, after which
  the unchanged spec 012 review route opens;
- safe refusal equivalence across missing, foreign, malformed, replayed, spent,
  and revoked resources, compared on status, body, and header set;
- accountant membership revocation and client session revocation between a
  rendered page and the next POST, both refusing before mutation with the
  concurrency version unchanged; store failure fails closed with no taxpayer
  response;
- one-way credential storage scanned against every value of every intake table,
  neutral transport filename, encrypted outside-root bytes, and scope-derived
  fingerprints that do not correlate across cases or firms;
- immutable answers, submissions, audit, and review association, including
  refused replacement and refused foreign/wrong-case records;
- no extraction, OCR/LLM, parsing, mapping, rounding, review-manufacturing,
  retention, or production-deployment capability in the source or runtime graph.
  The recording review repository throws on `SaveAsync`, so a manufacture attempt
  fails the suite rather than passing silently;
- schema additivity: no pending model changes against the SQL Server model, no
  `AlterColumn`/`AddColumn`/`Drop*`/`Rename*`/data-mutation operation in the
  intake migration, every created table an intake table, and the pre-existing
  firm, identity, and review tables intact.

## The one raw-byte exception

The authenticated encrypted source object outside the web root may contain a
SIN, and nothing in this task claims otherwise. It is protected by
unreachability: `IIntakeContentStore` declares no read member, no mapped route
serves it under five probed URL spellings, and no staged file contains a
plaintext probe. Every structured surface — browser models, HTML, URLs, cookies,
headers, SQL metadata, content keys, audit, logs, exceptions, diagnostics — is
asserted SIN-free in every form. Every taxpayer-shaped value in these suites is
assembled at test runtime and is obviously synthetic.

## Two test-expectation corrections made while writing these suites

Both were wrong expectations in the new tests, not product defects:

1. A masked Canadian SIN is three groups of three. The first probe used the 3-2-3
   shape a US SSN uses, which `IntakeDisplayNameGuard` correctly does not match.
   The probes are now `***-***-286` and `xxx-xxx-286`, both of which it rejects.
2. A rejected upload records its attempt and returns the fixed `400` invalid
   response, not `200`. The tests assert that, plus the fixed body.

## Still gated

Spec 014 completing moves no gate. No raw-content preview/read/download surface,
production content provider, Azure key ring, or deployment configuration ships;
the build still starts in Development only and may not be deployed anywhere that
can receive real taxpayer data. No source-document or intake-history retention or
purge rule was introduced and spec 011's review-record policy is unchanged. No
extraction ingress, OCR/LLM adapter, tax calculation, T1, NETFILE/EFILE,
taxpayer listing, value editing, review decision screen, export, provisioning,
second interactive component, global render mode, WebAssembly project, npm tree,
or third-party asset ships. Question F remains reserved.

Merging is a human-only step. This task neither merged nor approved its own PR.
